From 8b5ee5479bbeb302aca0e06c83add569be27ec86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Bayoumy <abayoumy@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:28:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] UI: ship English only and drop the language selector

The dashboard carried a full Korean translation, a second dictionary in the
image and a header button that switched between the two languages. The strip is
used in one language, so the Korean strings are gone (dictionary, every inline
KO/EN pair and the bilingual static fallbacks), English is the only language and
the selector plus its preference plumbing is removed:

- i18n.js keeps a single `en` dictionary. text(language,key,args) keeps its
  three-argument shape so every call site and the device-side compact builder
  stay valid; the language argument is now ignored.
- The KO arm of every inline ternary and the second argument of every
  text(ko,en)/logEvent(ko,en) helper is deleted, together with the helpers that
  no longer switch anything. The browser-session log keeps one message per row.
- index.html, ota-test.html and the OTA panel injected by build_assets.py are
  English; `#language` (button and CSS rule) is gone, and the device build's
  Korean fallback rewrites now map English preview text to English device text.
- The device build asserts that no gzip'd asset contains a Hangul character,
  next to the existing preview-text denylist, and the device dictionary is
  filtered as a single-language dictionary.
- settings: mttl_settings_default writes language=1 (English), so a fresh
  record starts English. The v8 record is unchanged: a stored 0 stays valid and
  loads normally (older records are not rejected), it simply renders English,
  and the dashboard always writes 1 when it saves. The device keeps reporting
  the byte in /api/config.
- The OTA controller keeps its English wording and no longer re-renders on a
  language toggle; its el('language') hook is gone.
- tests: the three node tests drop the language element and assert English
  wording.

Host checks are unchanged (249 checks).
